 among candidates that can be maintained hands-on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"The absorber must be one of the three materials listed in candidate_specs.md.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"candidate_specs.md lists Absorber-F1, Absorber-F2, and Absorber-F3; the recommendation is Absorber-F3.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"The energy resolution for 100 GeV electrons must be 4.5% or better.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The design uses the optimum thin sampling choice, 2 mm plates, for the dense dose-compliant candidate. This is the configuration selected to meet the 4.5% 100 GeV resolution requirement while respecting activation constraints.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"The residual dose rate at 1 m after one week of cooldown must not exceed 20 uSv/h.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"activation_study_2026.md reports Absorber-F3 at 12 uSv/h after one week of cooldown, below the 20 uSv/h limit. F2 is 85 uSv/h and is rejected; F1 is 6 uSv/h but offers worse expected resolution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Plate thickness between 2 and 10 mm.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Recommended plate thickness is 2 mm, which is within the allowed 2\u201310 mm range.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Finish by submitting one recommended material and plate thickness.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Submitted one recommendation: Absorber-F3 at 2 mm.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}", "call_id": "call_ac27483fdd8447c9ab816a0596d1cd6e", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_087b0d8de3bd3ab3006b02dcef64b887d0b9054b973f92b358", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
